From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] evr: presenter display control, rate support, statistics, quality advise, messages, position mapper

The default video presenter (MFCreateVideoPresenter) had these as E_NOTIMPL stubs:

- IMFVideoDisplayControl: Set/GetBorderColor (black by default), SetRenderingPrefs
  (E_INVALIDARG outside the defined flags), GetIdealVideoSize (the native size,
  E_POINTER for two NULLs, MF_E_SHUTDOWN), RepaintVideo (shows the last frame
  again, not counted as a new frame). Set/GetFullscreen stay E_NOTIMPL, the
  documented answer, without the FIXME.
- IMFRateSupport: GetFastestRate and IsRateSupported (display refresh rate over
  the frame rate, unlimited when thinning or with no frame rate, MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_RATE
  with the nearest supported rate, MF_E_SHUTDOWN).
- IQualProp: FramesDroppedInRenderer, AvgFrameRate, Jitter, AvgSyncOffset,
  DevSyncOffset next to FramesDrawn: available while the clock runs (E_NOTIMPL
  otherwise, E_POINTER for NULL), counted from the frames actually presented and
  reset when the clock stops.
- IMFQualityAdvise / IMFQualityAdviseLimits: the presenter shows every frame, so
  only "none" and "normal" are accepted (what the conformance tests expect).
- IMFClockStateSink::OnClockSetRate: S_OK, the rate is kept.
- ProcessMessage: FLUSH discards the queued frames, STEP and CANCELSTEP are
  accepted, MF_E_SHUTDOWN after shutdown; undefined messages stay E_NOTIMPL.
- IMFVideoPositionMapper: maps a window coordinate into the visible part of the
  video and on through the mixer's mapper.
- IMFGetService: an unknown service is MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE without a FIXME.

The conformance tests' todo_wine marks that pass now are removed.
